{"study_accession":"PRJNA767844","secondary_study_accession":"SRP339660","title":"Pre-neoplastic somatic mutations including MYD88L265P in lymphoplasmacytic lymphoma [scRNA-seq]","description":"Normal-cell counterparts of solid and myeloid tumors accumulate mutations years before disease onset; whether this occurs in B-lymphocytes prior to lymphoma remains uncertain. We sequenced multiple stages of the B-lineage in elderly individuals and patients with lymphoplasmacytic lymphoma, a singular disease for studying lymphomagenesis because of high-prevalence of mutated MYD88. We observed similar accumulation of random mutations in B-lineages from both cohorts and, unexpectedly, found MYD88L265P in normal precursor and mature B-lymphocytes from lymphoma patients. We uncovered genetic and transcriptional pathways driving malignant transformation and leveraged these to model lymphoplasmacytic lymphoma in mice, based on mutated MYD88 in B-cell precursors and BCL2 overexpression. Thus, MYD88L265P is a pre-neoplastic event, which challenges current understanding of lymphomagenesis and may have implications for early detection of B-cell lymphomas. Overall design: single-cell RNA and BCR sequencing (scRNA/BCRseq) in a total of 40,169 B cells and PCs from three patients with IgM MGUS and two with LPL/WM","pubmed":"35044826","geo_series":"","n_samples":10,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN21973412","study_accession":"PRJNA767844","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"IgM_MGUS_1 [scRNA-seq]","description":"IgM_MGUS_1 [scRNA-seq]","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5607191","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-11-06","attributes":[["source_name","Bone marrow_IgM_MGUS"],["cell_type","B and plasma cells"],["tissue","Bone marrow"],["subject status","patients with IgM MGUS"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR16151308","experiment_accession":"SRX12436178","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2000","read_co